# Brand Theme

Single source of truth: `src/theme/tokens.ts`. App imports: `src/theme` (`chart`, `colors`, `brand`, `gradients`, `shadows`). Tailwind loads tokens via root `theme-tokens.cjs` (kept outside `src/` so Vite never serves CJS to the browser).

## Changing the brand

1. Edit scales / aliases in `src/theme/tokens.ts` only
2. Mirror CSS vars in `src/index.css` if hex values changed
3. Restart Vite; run `npm run lint:ui`

Do **not** scatter new hex values across pages.

## Prefer in new UI

```tsx
// ✅ semantic Tailwind
className="bg-primary-500 text-white shadow-brand dark:bg-secondary-900"

// ✅ charts / SVG / canvas
import { chart } from '../theme';
stroke={chart.primary}

// ❌ invent hex or old indigo/blue palette
style={{ color: '#6366F1' }}
className="bg-[#0f0f23]"
```

Use `primary-*`, `secondary-*`, `accent-*`, `bg-brand-gradient`, `shadow-brand`. Prefer semantic names over remapped `blue-*` / `purple-*` in new code.

## Banned

Hardcoded off-brand hex: `#6366F1`, `#4F46E5`, `#3B82F6`, `#2563EB`, `#8B5CF6`, `#7C3AED`, `#A855F7`, `#0F0F23`, `#1A1A3E`, `#020617`, `#0B1120`, `#060B14`, `#0B1221`.

## Exceptions

- Partner greens: M-Pesa, WhatsApp logos/accents
- True semantic success/error/warning when meaning requires it
- Code-editor mock surfaces (`#0d1117`) when imitating GitHub
